Modifications are summarised below.

Modifications to the original model
-------------------------------------

  A (decay parameter)
    Original:  fixed learnable scalar per head — nn.Parameter A_log of shape
               (nheads,); decay computed as -exp(A_log), constant across tokens.
    Modified:  data-dependent per-token per-head value — dd_A is projected from
               the input via in_proj and decay is computed as -softplus(dd_A),
               yielding a distinct decay value at each sequence position.

  MIMO rank-R state update
    Original:  SISO only — state update is a rank-1 outer product B ⊗ x.
    Modified:  Generalised to rank-R MIMO via ssd_mimo(); the state update
               becomes a sum of R outer products Σ_r B[:,r] ⊗ x[:,r].
               mimo_rank=1 recovers the original SISO behaviour exactly.

  Partial RoPE (rope_fraction)
    Original:  RoPE applied to all d_state dimensions of B and C.
    Modified:  RoPE applied only to the first d_state * rope_fraction dimensions
               (rope_fraction=0.5 by default); remaining dims are unrotated.

  B_bias / C_bias initialisation
    Original:  Initialised to 1.0 as recommended in the paper.
    Modified:  Initialised to 0.02 for training stability at higher learning
               rates (empirically validated).

  SSD internal precision
    Original:  Assumed float32 inputs throughout ssd_siso().
    Modified:  ssd_siso() and ssd_mimo() cast inputs to float32 internally and
               cast outputs back to the original dtype, enabling correct
               operation with bfloat16 inputs.
